IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-associates`

-- Tests for sfa-associates.
-- Expected values are written from the text of the Act (the quote lines in the module under test), never from its output.

-- within paragraph (a) alone
#ASSERT (`s 3(1) the person is associated with the other person` WITH `the context of the provision otherwise requires a different meaning` IS FALSE, `the person is within paragraph (a) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST TRUE), `the person is within paragraph (b) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (c) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (d) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (e) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (f) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (g) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is taken to be associated by virtue of paragraph (b), (c), (e) or (f) despite section 3(3)` IS (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- within paragraph (d) alone
#ASSERT (`s 3(1) the person is associated with the other person` WITH `the context of the provision otherwise requires a different meaning` IS FALSE, `the person is within paragraph (a) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (b) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (c) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (d) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST TRUE), `the person is within paragraph (e) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (f) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (g) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is taken to be associated by virtue of paragraph (b), (c), (e) or (f) despite section 3(3)` IS (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- within paragraph (g) alone
#ASSERT (`s 3(1) the person is associated with the other person` WITH `the context of the provision otherwise requires a different meaning` IS FALSE, `the person is within paragraph (a) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (b) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (c) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (d) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (e) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (f) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (g) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST TRUE), `the person is taken to be associated by virtue of paragraph (b), (c), (e) or (f) despite section 3(3)` IS (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- within paragraph (b), and section 3(3) does not take it away
#ASSERT (`s 3(1) the person is associated with the other person` WITH `the context of the provision otherwise requires a different meaning` IS FALSE, `the person is within paragraph (a) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (b) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST TRUE), `the person is within paragraph (c) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (d) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (e) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (f) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (g) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is taken to be associated by virtue of paragraph (b), (c), (e) or (f) despite section 3(3)` IS NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- within paragraph (b) only by reason of the section 3(3) circumstances: "is not taken to be associated"
#ASSERT (`s 3(1) the person is associated with the other person` WITH `the context of the provision otherwise requires a different meaning` IS FALSE, `the person is within paragraph (a) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (b) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST TRUE), `the person is within paragraph (c) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (d) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (e) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (f) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (g) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is taken to be associated by virtue of paragraph (b), (c), (e) or (f) despite section 3(3)` IS (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
