#ASSERT (`s 3(1) the person is associated with the other person` WITH `the context of the provision otherwise requires a different meaning` IS FALSE, `the person is within paragraph (a) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (b) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (c) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (d) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (e) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST TRUE), `the person is within paragraph (f) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (g) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is taken to be associated by virtue of paragraph (b), (c), (e) or (f) despite section 3(3)` IS (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- within paragraph (f), and section 3(3) does not take it away
#ASSERT (`s 3(1) the person is associated with the other person` WITH `the context of the provision otherwise requires a different meaning` IS FALSE, `the person is within paragraph (a) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (b) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (c) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (d) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (e) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (f) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST TRUE), `the person is within paragraph (g) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is taken to be associated by virtue of paragraph (b), (c), (e) or (f) despite section 3(3)` IS NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- within paragraph (f) only by reason of the section 3(3) circumstances: "is not taken to be associated"
#ASSERT (`s 3(1) the person is associated with the other person` WITH `the context of the provision otherwise requires a different meaning` IS FALSE, `the person is within paragraph (a) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (b) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (c) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (d) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (e) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (f) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST TRUE), `the person is within paragraph (g) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is taken to be associated by virtue of paragraph (b), (c), (e) or (f) despite section 3(3)` IS (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- paragraph (b) is taken away by section 3(3), but paragraph (a) is met independently
#ASSERT (`s 3(1) the person is associated with the other person` WITH `the context of the provision otherwise requires a different meaning` IS FALSE, `the person is within paragraph (a) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST TRUE), `the person is within paragraph (b) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST TRUE), `the person is within paragraph (c) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (d) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (e) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (f) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (g) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is taken to be associated by virtue of paragraph (b), (c), (e) or (f) despite section 3(3)` IS (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- paragraph (b) is taken away, but the caller could not answer paragraph (c)
#ASSERT (`s 3(1) the person is associated with the other person` WITH `the context of the provision otherwise requires a different meaning` IS FALSE, `the person is within paragraph (a) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (b) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST TRUE), `the person is within paragraph (c) of section 3(1)` IS NOTHING, `the person is within paragraph (d) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (e) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (f) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (g) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is taken to be associated by virtue of paragraph (b), (c), (e) or (f) despite section 3(3)` IS (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- a limb not answered: NOTHING, never FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 3(1) the person is associated with the other person` WITH `the context of the provision otherwise requires a different meaning` IS FALSE, `the person is within paragraph (a) of section 3(1)` IS NOTHING, `the person is within paragraph (b) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (c) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (d) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (e) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (f) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (g) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is taken to be associated by virtue of paragraph (b), (c), (e) or (f) despite section 3(3)` IS (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- no limb: "is a reference to" closes the list
#ASSERT (`s 3(1) the person is associated with the other person` WITH `the context of the provision otherwise requires a different meaning` IS FALSE, `the person is within paragraph (a) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (b) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (c) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (d) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (e) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (f) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (g) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is taken to be associated by virtue of paragraph (b), (c), (e) or (f) despite section 3(3)` IS (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "Unless the context otherwise requires": the definition does not decide
#ASSERT (`s 3(1) the person is associated with the other person` WITH `the context of the provision otherwise requires a different meaning` IS TRUE, `the person is within paragraph (a) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST TRUE), `the person is within paragraph (b) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (c) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (d) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (e) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (f) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is within paragraph (g) of section 3(1)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the person is taken to be associated by virtue of paragraph (b), (c), (e) or (f) despite section 3(3)` IS (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS NOTHING

-- the other person is a corporation and the person is within (a)(the person is a director or secretary of the corporation)
#ASSERT (`s 3(1)(a) the person is a director, secretary or related corporation of the corporation` WITH `the other person is a corporation` IS TRUE, `the person is a director or secretary of the corporation` IS TRUE, `the person is a related corporation of the corporation` IS FALSE, `the person is a director or secretary of a related corporation of the corporation` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the other person is a corporation and the person is within (a)(the person is a related corporation of the corporation)
#ASSERT (`s 3(1)(a) the person is a director, secretary or related corporation of the corporation` WITH `the other person is a corporation` IS TRUE, `the person is a director or secretary of the corporation` IS FALSE, `the person is a related corporation of the corporation` IS TRUE, `the person is a director or secretary of a related corporation of the corporation` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the other person is a corporation and the person is within (a)(the person is a director or secretary of a related corporation of the corporation)
#ASSERT (`s 3(1)(a) the person is a director, secretary or related corporation of the corporation` WITH `the other person is a corporation` IS TRUE, `the person is a director or secretary of the corporation` IS FALSE, `the person is a related corporation of the corporation` IS FALSE, `the person is a director or secretary of a related corporation of the corporation` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a) applies only where the other person is a corporation
#ASSERT (`s 3(1)(a) the person is a director, secretary or related corporation of the corporation` WITH `the other person is a corporation` IS FALSE, `the person is a director or secretary of the corporation` IS TRUE, `the person is a related corporation of the corporation` IS FALSE, `the person is a director or secretary of a related corporation of the corporation` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a corporation, but the person is none of (i) to (iii)
#ASSERT (`s 3(1)(a) the person is a director, secretary or related corporation of the corporation` WITH `the other person is a corporation` IS TRUE, `the person is a director or secretary of the corporation` IS FALSE, `the person is a related corporation of the corporation` IS FALSE, `the person is a director or secretary of a related corporation of the corporation` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- an agreement about voting power: limb (b)(by reason of it either of them may exercise or control, or substantially influence, the voting power attached to a share in the corporation)
#ASSERT (`s 3(1)(b) the person has an agreement about voting power with the other person` WITH `the matter is the extent of a power to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the voting power attached to voting shares in a corporation` IS TRUE, `the person has, or proposes to enter into with the other person, an agreement, arrangement, understanding or undertaking` IS TRUE, `by reason of it either of them may exercise or control, or substantially influence, the voting power attached to a share in the corporation` IS TRUE, `it is made with a view to controlling or influencing the composition of the board of directors, or the conduct of affairs, of the corporation` IS FALSE, `under it either of them may acquire shares in the corporation from the other, or may be required to dispose of such shares as the other directs` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an agreement about voting power: limb (b)(it is made with a view to controlling or influencing the composition of the board of directors, or the conduct of affairs, of the corporation)
#ASSERT (`s 3(1)(b) the person has an agreement about voting power with the other person` WITH `the matter is the extent of a power to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the voting power attached to voting shares in a corporation` IS TRUE, `the person has, or proposes to enter into with the other person, an agreement, arrangement, understanding or undertaking` IS TRUE, `by reason of it either of them may exercise or control, or substantially influence, the voting power attached to a share in the corporation` IS FALSE, `it is made with a view to controlling or influencing the composition of the board of directors, or the conduct of affairs, of the corporation` IS TRUE, `under it either of them may acquire shares in the corporation from the other, or may be required to dispose of such shares as the other directs` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an agreement about voting power: limb (b)(under it either of them may acquire shares in the corporation from the other, or may be required to dispose of such shares as the other directs)
#ASSERT (`s 3(1)(b) the person has an agreement about voting power with the other person` WITH `the matter is the extent of a power to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the voting power attached to voting shares in a corporation` IS TRUE, `the person has, or proposes to enter into with the other person, an agreement, arrangement, understanding or undertaking` IS TRUE, `by reason of it either of them may exercise or control, or substantially influence, the voting power attached to a share in the corporation` IS FALSE, `it is made with a view to controlling or influencing the composition of the board of directors, or the conduct of affairs, of the corporation` IS FALSE, `under it either of them may acquire shares in the corporation from the other, or may be required to dispose of such shares as the other directs` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an agreement, but none of (i) to (iii)
#ASSERT (`s 3(1)(b) the person has an agreement about voting power with the other person` WITH `the matter is the extent of a power to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the voting power attached to voting shares in a corporation` IS TRUE, `the person has, or proposes to enter into with the other person, an agreement, arrangement, understanding or undertaking` IS TRUE, `by reason of it either of them may exercise or control, or substantially influence, the voting power attached to a share in the corporation` IS FALSE, `it is made with a view to controlling or influencing the composition of the board of directors, or the conduct of affairs, of the corporation` IS FALSE, `under it either of them may acquire shares in the corporation from the other, or may be required to dispose of such shares as the other directs` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no agreement, arrangement, understanding or undertaking
#ASSERT (`s 3(1)(b) the person has an agreement about voting power with the other person` WITH `the matter is the extent of a power to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the voting power attached to voting shares in a corporation` IS TRUE, `the person has, or proposes to enter into with the other person, an agreement, arrangement, understanding or undertaking` IS FALSE, `by reason of it either of them may exercise or control, or substantially influence, the voting power attached to a share in the corporation` IS TRUE, `it is made with a view to controlling or influencing the composition of the board of directors, or the conduct of affairs, of the corporation` IS FALSE, `under it either of them may acquire shares in the corporation from the other, or may be required to dispose of such shares as the other directs` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) applies only where the matter is the extent of a power over voting power: for another matter see (d)
#ASSERT (`s 3(1)(b) the person has an agreement about voting power with the other person` WITH `the matter is the extent of a power to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the voting power attached to voting shares in a corporation` IS FALSE, `the person has, or proposes to enter into with the other person, an agreement, arrangement, understanding or undertaking` IS TRUE, `by reason of it either of them may exercise or control, or substantially influence, the voting power attached to a share in the corporation` IS TRUE, `it is made with a view to controlling or influencing the composition of the board of directors, or the conduct of affairs, of the corporation` IS FALSE, `under it either of them may acquire shares in the corporation from the other, or may be required to dispose of such shares as the other directs` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- in a matter relating to shares in a corporation, a person may be an associate of the corporation and the corporation may be an associate of a person
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(b) a corporation may be an associate in a matter relating to shares` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a matter not relating to shares: the exception does not speak
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(b) a corporation may be an associate in a matter relating to shares` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- acting in concert in relation to the matter
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(c) the person is acting in concert with the other person` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not acting, or proposing to act, in concert
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(c) the person is acting in concert with the other person` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- alleged in proceedings and knowledge not proved: not considered associated
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the director is considered associated with the other person in the proceedings` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- knowledge proved: the bar is lifted and (1)(d)(i) decides
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the director is considered associated with the other person in the proceedings` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- not an allegation in proceedings: subsection (2) does not speak
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the director is considered associated with the other person in the proceedings` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- not in proceedings
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the director is considered associated with the other person in the proceedings` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (d)(i): a fellow director, no proceedings
#ASSERT (`s 3(1)(d) the person is a fellow director or a trustee connected with the other person` WITH `the matter is a matter other than the extent of a power to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the voting power attached to voting shares in a corporation` IS TRUE, `the person is a director of a corporation of which the other person is a director` IS TRUE, `it is alleged in proceedings under this Act that the person was associated with the other person as a fellow director at a particular time` IS FALSE, `the person alleging the association proves that the person at that time knew or ought reasonably to have known the material particulars of the matter` IS FALSE, `the person is a trustee of a trust` IS FALSE, `the other person benefits, or is capable of benefiting, from the trust otherwise than by reason of transactions entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (d)(i) subject to (2): alleged in proceedings, knowledge not proved
#ASSERT (`s 3(1)(d) the person is a fellow director or a trustee connected with the other person` WITH `the matter is a matter other than the extent of a power to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the voting power attached to voting shares in a corporation` IS TRUE, `the person is a director of a corporation of which the other person is a director` IS TRUE, `it is alleged in proceedings under this Act that the person was associated with the other person as a fellow director at a particular time` IS TRUE, `the person alleging the association proves that the person at that time knew or ought reasonably to have known the material particulars of the matter` IS FALSE, `the person is a trustee of a trust` IS FALSE, `the other person benefits, or is capable of benefiting, from the trust otherwise than by reason of transactions entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (d)(i) subject to (2): knowledge proved
#ASSERT (`s 3(1)(d) the person is a fellow director or a trustee connected with the other person` WITH `the matter is a matter other than the extent of a power to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the voting power attached to voting shares in a corporation` IS TRUE, `the person is a director of a corporation of which the other person is a director` IS TRUE, `it is alleged in proceedings under this Act that the person was associated with the other person as a fellow director at a particular time` IS TRUE, `the person alleging the association proves that the person at that time knew or ought reasonably to have known the material particulars of the matter` IS TRUE, `the person is a trustee of a trust` IS FALSE, `the other person benefits, or is capable of benefiting, from the trust otherwise than by reason of transactions entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (d)(ii): a trustee of a trust the other person benefits from
#ASSERT (`s 3(1)(d) the person is a fellow director or a trustee connected with the other person` WITH `the matter is a matter other than the extent of a power to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the voting power attached to voting shares in a corporation` IS TRUE, `the person is a director of a corporation of which the other person is a director` IS FALSE, `it is alleged in proceedings under this Act that the person was associated with the other person as a fellow director at a particular time` IS FALSE, `the person alleging the association proves that the person at that time knew or ought reasonably to have known the material particulars of the matter` IS FALSE, `the person is a trustee of a trust` IS TRUE, `the other person benefits, or is capable of benefiting, from the trust otherwise than by reason of transactions entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (d)(ii): the other person does not benefit otherwise than through ordinary lending transactions
#ASSERT (`s 3(1)(d) the person is a fellow director or a trustee connected with the other person` WITH `the matter is a matter other than the extent of a power to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the voting power attached to voting shares in a corporation` IS TRUE, `the person is a director of a corporation of which the other person is a director` IS FALSE, `it is alleged in proceedings under this Act that the person was associated with the other person as a fellow director at a particular time` IS FALSE, `the person alleging the association proves that the person at that time knew or ought reasonably to have known the material particulars of the matter` IS FALSE, `the person is a trustee of a trust` IS TRUE, `the other person benefits, or is capable of benefiting, from the trust otherwise than by reason of transactions entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2) bars only (d)(i); a trustee route is untouched
#ASSERT (`s 3(1)(d) the person is a fellow director or a trustee connected with the other person` WITH `the matter is a matter other than the extent of a power to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the voting power attached to voting shares in a corporation` IS TRUE, `the person is a director of a corporation of which the other person is a director` IS FALSE, `it is alleged in proceedings under this Act that the person was associated with the other person as a fellow director at a particular time` IS TRUE, `the person alleging the association proves that the person at that time knew or ought reasonably to have known the material particulars of the matter` IS FALSE, `the person is a trustee of a trust` IS TRUE, `the other person benefits, or is capable of benefiting, from the trust otherwise than by reason of transactions entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (d) applies only to a matter other than the extent of a power over voting power
#ASSERT (`s 3(1)(d) the person is a fellow director or a trustee connected with the other person` WITH `the matter is a matter other than the extent of a power to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the voting power attached to voting shares in a corporation` IS FALSE, `the person is a director of a corporation of which the other person is a director` IS TRUE, `it is alleged in proceedings under this Act that the person was associated with the other person as a fellow director at a particular time` IS FALSE, `the person alleging the association proves that the person at that time knew or ought reasonably to have known the material particulars of the matter` IS FALSE, `the person is a trustee of a trust` IS FALSE, `the other person benefits, or is capable of benefiting, from the trust otherwise than by reason of transactions entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- neither (i) nor (ii)
#ASSERT (`s 3(1)(d) the person is a fellow director or a trustee connected with the other person` WITH `the matter is a matter other than the extent of a power to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the voting power attached to voting shares in a corporation` IS TRUE, `the person is a director of a corporation of which the other person is a director` IS FALSE, `it is alleged in proceedings under this Act that the person was associated with the other person as a fellow director at a particular time` IS FALSE, `the person alleging the association proves that the person at that time knew or ought reasonably to have known the material particulars of the matter` IS FALSE, `the person is a trustee of a trust` IS FALSE, `the other person benefits, or is capable of benefiting, from the trust otherwise than by reason of transactions entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- the subsidiary legislation says so
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(e) subsidiary legislation regards the person as associated with the other person` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no such subsidiary legislation
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(e) subsidiary legislation regards the person as associated with the other person` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- associated, formally or informally, in some other way
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(f) the person is associated with the other person in another way` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not associated in any way
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(f) the person is associated with the other person in another way` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- an act done with a view to becoming associated
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(g) the other person has acted with a view to becoming associated with the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an act, but not with that view
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(g) the other person has acted with a view to becoming associated with the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a view, but no transaction, act or thing
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(g) the other person has acted with a view to becoming associated with the person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- advice or agency in the proper performance of professional or business functions
#ASSERT `s 3(3)(a) the circumstance is that one of the persons provides advice to, or acts for, the other in a professional or business capacity` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not in the proper performance of those functions
#ASSERT `s 3(3)(a) the circumstance is that one of the persons provides advice to, or acts for, the other in a professional or business capacity` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no advice given or acting for A
#ASSERT `s 3(3)(a) the circumstance is that one of the persons provides advice to, or acts for, the other in a professional or business capacity` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- all three elements
#ASSERT `s 3(3)(b) the circumstance is that a customer gives specific instructions to a dealer to acquire shares` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not instructions to acquire shares in the ordinary course
#ASSERT `s 3(3)(b) the circumstance is that a customer gives specific instructions to a dealer to acquire shares` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A does not ordinarily deal in capital markets products
#ASSERT `s 3(3)(b) the circumstance is that a customer gives specific instructions to a dealer to acquire shares` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no instructions given
#ASSERT `s 3(3)(b) the circumstance is that a customer gives specific instructions to a dealer to acquire shares` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- a take-over offer in relation to shares held by A
#ASSERT `s 3(3)(c) the circumstance is that one of the persons has sent or proposes to send the other a take-over offer` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- offers under a take-over announcement in relation to shares held by A
#ASSERT `s 3(3)(c) the circumstance is that one of the persons has sent or proposes to send the other a take-over offer` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not in relation to shares held by A
#ASSERT `s 3(3)(c) the circumstance is that one of the persons has sent or proposes to send the other a take-over offer` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- neither a take-over offer nor an announcement
#ASSERT `s 3(3)(c) the circumstance is that one of the persons has sent or proposes to send the other a take-over offer` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- appointed as proxy for no consideration from A or A's associate
#ASSERT `s 3(3)(d) the circumstance is that one of the persons has appointed the other as proxy or representative` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- for valuable consideration given by A or an associate of A
#ASSERT `s 3(3)(d) the circumstance is that one of the persons has appointed the other as proxy or representative` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no appointment
#ASSERT `s 3(3)(d) the circumstance is that one of the persons has appointed the other as proxy or representative` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- only the professional or business circumstance (a): not taken to be associated
#ASSERT (`s 3(3) the person is taken to be associated by virtue of subsection (1)(b), (c), (e) or (f)` WITH `the circumstance in paragraph (a) of section 3(3) is present` IS (JUST TRUE), `the circumstance in paragraph (b) of section 3(3) is present` IS (JUST FALSE), `the circumstance in paragraph (c) of section 3(3) is present` IS (JUST FALSE), `the circumstance in paragraph (d) of section 3(3) is present` IS (JUST FALSE), `the association rests on some ground other than the circumstances in paragraphs (a) to (d) of section 3(3)` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- only the customer instruction (b)
#ASSERT (`s 3(3) the person is taken to be associated by virtue of subsection (1)(b), (c), (e) or (f)` WITH `the circumstance in paragraph (a) of section 3(3) is present` IS (JUST FALSE), `the circumstance in paragraph (b) of section 3(3) is present` IS (JUST TRUE), `the circumstance in paragraph (c) of section 3(3) is present` IS (JUST FALSE), `the circumstance in paragraph (d) of section 3(3) is present` IS (JUST FALSE), `the association rests on some ground other than the circumstances in paragraphs (a) to (d) of section 3(3)` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- only the take-over offer (c)
#ASSERT (`s 3(3) the person is taken to be associated by virtue of subsection (1)(b), (c), (e) or (f)` WITH `the circumstance in paragraph (a) of section 3(3) is present` IS (JUST FALSE), `the circumstance in paragraph (b) of section 3(3) is present` IS (JUST FALSE), `the circumstance in paragraph (c) of section 3(3) is present` IS (JUST TRUE), `the circumstance in paragraph (d) of section 3(3) is present` IS (JUST FALSE), `the association rests on some ground other than the circumstances in paragraphs (a) to (d) of section 3(3)` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- only the proxy appointment (d)
#ASSERT (`s 3(3) the person is taken to be associated by virtue of subsection (1)(b), (c), (e) or (f)` WITH `the circumstance in paragraph (a) of section 3(3) is present` IS (JUST FALSE), `the circumstance in paragraph (b) of section 3(3) is present` IS (JUST FALSE), `the circumstance in paragraph (c) of section 3(3) is present` IS (JUST FALSE), `the circumstance in paragraph (d) of section 3(3) is present` IS (JUST TRUE), `the association rests on some ground other than the circumstances in paragraphs (a) to (d) of section 3(3)` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "one or more of the following": two circumstances together
#ASSERT (`s 3(3) the person is taken to be associated by virtue of subsection (1)(b), (c), (e) or (f)` WITH `the circumstance in paragraph (a) of section 3(3) is present` IS (JUST TRUE), `the circumstance in paragraph (b) of section 3(3) is present` IS (JUST FALSE), `the circumstance in paragraph (c) of section 3(3) is present` IS (JUST TRUE), `the circumstance in paragraph (d) of section 3(3) is present` IS (JUST FALSE), `the association rests on some ground other than the circumstances in paragraphs (a) to (d) of section 3(3)` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the association rests on another ground as well: "by reason only of" is not met
#ASSERT (`s 3(3) the person is taken to be associated by virtue of subsection (1)(b), (c), (e) or (f)` WITH `the circumstance in paragraph (a) of section 3(3) is present` IS (JUST TRUE), `the circumstance in paragraph (b) of section 3(3) is present` IS (JUST FALSE), `the circumstance in paragraph (c) of section 3(3) is present` IS (JUST FALSE), `the circumstance in paragraph (d) of section 3(3) is present` IS (JUST FALSE), `the association rests on some ground other than the circumstances in paragraphs (a) to (d) of section 3(3)` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- a circumstance the caller could not answer
#ASSERT (`s 3(3) the person is taken to be associated by virtue of subsection (1)(b), (c), (e) or (f)` WITH `the circumstance in paragraph (a) of section 3(3) is present` IS NOTHING, `the circumstance in paragraph (b) of section 3(3) is present` IS (JUST FALSE), `the circumstance in paragraph (c) of section 3(3) is present` IS (JUST FALSE), `the circumstance in paragraph (d) of section 3(3) is present` IS (JUST FALSE), `the association rests on some ground other than the circumstances in paragraphs (a) to (d) of section 3(3)` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- no circumstance present
#ASSERT (`s 3(3) the person is taken to be associated by virtue of subsection (1)(b), (c), (e) or (f)` WITH `the circumstance in paragraph (a) of section 3(3) is present` IS (JUST FALSE), `the circumstance in paragraph (b) of section 3(3) is present` IS (JUST FALSE), `the circumstance in paragraph (c) of section 3(3) is present` IS (JUST FALSE), `the circumstance in paragraph (d) of section 3(3) is present` IS (JUST FALSE), `the association rests on some ground other than the circumstances in paragraphs (a) to (d) of section 3(3)` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
